Update the handler passed to `setThrowInvalidWriteToSignalError` so it accepts the signal node.

**Before/after:**
```ts
// before (19.1)
setThrowInvalidWriteToSignalError(() => { throw new Error('write to signal'); });
// after (19.2)
setThrowInvalidWriteToSignalError(<T>(node: SignalNode<T>) => { throw new Error(`write to signal: ${node}`); });
```

Replace explicit `ResourceOptions<T, R>` declarations with `PromiseResourceOptions<T, R>` from `@angular/core`.

**Before/after:**
```ts
// before (19.1)
export interface MyResourceOptions<T, R> extends ResourceOptions<T, R> {}

// after (19.2)
export interface MyResourceOptions<T, R> extends PromiseResourceOptions<T, R> {}
```

Where `RxResourceOptions<T, R>` is explicitly extended or referenced as base, use `BaseResourceOptions<T, R>` from `@angular/core`.

**Before/after:**
```ts
// before (19.1)
export interface RxResourceOptions<T, R> extends Omit<ResourceOptions<T, R>, 'loader'> { ... }

// after (19.2)
export interface RxResourceOptions<T, R> extends BaseResourceOptions<T, R> { loader: (params: ResourceLoaderParams<R>) => Observable<T>; }
```
